note: "Round 1 was FAIL on four verified findings, all fixed in 9164ed7 and re-verified empirically on this tip.
  (1) htmldoc-id read the attribute from anywhere in the document; the runtime reads document.documentElement, so
  an id on a stray div with none on <html> passed green while the comment and diff layers stayed dead. Now read
  from the <html> node, case-insensitively.
  (2) htmldoc-bootstrap matched any src ending in the filename, so a local ./vendor/htmldoc.js - which serves no
  doc.css - passed. Now the canonical URL exactly; re-verified that query-string, http and whitespace variants
  all red and that no real doc uses one.
  (3) DESIGN BLOCKER: the W10 proof run claimed visual-weight-follows-goals and ordering-by-priority satisfied
  while its own Layout sketch and mockup mount order still rendered guidance first - the Tune call was recorded
  and never applied, and the review row re-listed it as pending. Fixed by applying the tune call across the
  sketch, the mounts, the interaction deltas and the capabilities table, and adding the loop-back declaration the
  Tune template requires. Both receipt claims are now true of the artifact. Tier-1 could not see this: it checks a
  receipt is complete, never that it is true.
  (4) The predicates bind governed docs only - 37 of 99. The 62 ungoverned T1/T2 pages keep the layer by
  convention and all 62 currently carry it. Left open deliberately: widening it breaks the hooks' standing promise
  that an ungoverned doc is silent, a contract change owed its own WU and a decision record.
  Refuted: three efficiency findings targeting pre-existing code the diff never touches (nodes() re-tokenising,
  check_uppercase_mute_labels, check_colour_plus_text); blob_of/read_utf8_at as parallel implementations (one
  returns a hash, the other content); run #7's generous-targets inherited verdict (two of three cited components
  are real and TSDoc-proven, and the rule binds at component level); the Tune why-block as a mandatory cell (it is
  an unenforced template convention, and tune-drawn does not check it).
  Gate 0 green. 210 unit + 64 integration + 4 e2e. 99 docs, 0 red."
